"voice": "<k>voice_preset</k>: <v>'cornerman'</v>  (warmth <v>5</v> · humor <v>3</v> · directness <v>3</v> · energy <v>4</v>)\n<k>stance_school</k>: <v>polarized</v>\n<k>emphasis</k>: Data↔Sentiment <v>3</v> (balanced) · Process↔Outcome <v>3</v> (balanced)\n<k>corpus.school.stance</k>: \"Keep easy days easy and hard days genuinely hard; the moderate middle is where progress goes to hide.\"",
"llmcall": "<k>prompt_id</k>: <v>coach_message_v9</v> · <k>schema</k>: <v>2.0</v>\n<k>message</k>: \"Good spin to end the evening. Forty minutes at a genuinely easy effort — RPE 3, heart rate comfortable throughout — and you kept it exactly where an easy session should live. Without GPS there's not a lot of mechanical detail to pull from this ride, but the effort picture is clear: relaxed, controlled, no drama. That's the job done. The ride itself is fine. Where it gets more interesting is the wider context around it. Your condition right now is actually in a decent place — fitness solid, fatigue well managed, form sitting on the fresh side. But the week's training load has come in well below your normal level, around 35% down on effort versus your norm. And separately, across your recent easy sessions there's a small efficiency dip developing — roughly 15% below where it was a few sessions back. Both of those things are probably connected; a lighter load week tends to do that. If this has been a deliberate pullback or recovery block, that makes total sense. If it hasn't been intentional, it's worth knowing about. Here's what I'd focus on: you've got fresh legs and a real fitness base to work with right now. This is the moment to put one proper quality session in — a genuine threshold effort, or some interval work with real teeth to it. Something that earns the easy days around it. All easy and no hard means you're not getting the sharpening stimulus that makes the easy work actually pay off. That contrast is where progress lives, and right now you're running without it. One thing for planning: you've mentioned the Lisdexamfetamine peaks HR between roughly 12–3pm. Tonight's ride was well clear of that window, so this HR read is probably clean — but when you're slotting in a harder session, earlier morning or later evening gives you a more honest picture of where you actually are. Has this been a deliberate lighter week, or just how it's landed?\"",
