"voice": "<k>voice_preset</k>: <v>'cornerman'</v>  (warmth <v>5</v> · humor <v>3</v> · directness <v>3</v> · energy <v>4</v>)\n<k>stance_school</k>: <v>polarized</v>\n<k>emphasis</k>: Data↔Sentiment <v>3</v> (balanced) · Process↔Outcome <v>1</v> (strongly Process)\n<k>corpus.school.stance</k>: \"Durability is built by lots of easy aerobic running; the long game beats any single sharp session.\"",
"llmcall": "<k>prompt_id</k>: <v>coach_message_v6</v> · <k>schema</k>: <v>2.0</v>\n<k>message</k>: \"Dear Reader, your correspondent must confess she arrived at this column expecting at minimum a scandal — or, failing that, something worthy of comment. She found neither. Thirty-two minutes in the weight room, an average heart rate of 112, an RPE of 3: a session so thoroughly unremarkable that committing it to ink feels almost impolite. And yet propriety demands it. What can be said is this: it was exactly right. You kept easy, easy — for the second time today, no less, following this afternoon's earlier walk. The load score sits at a trivial 35.4, not a single risk flag was raised, and your felt effort aligned neatly with what the heart rate showed. For someone with sixteen activities on the ledger this week, keeping each individual session genuinely within conversational range is not a small discipline. It is, in fact, the work — and you are doing it. Your form sits in modestly positive territory at the moment, which is to say the week's volume has not yet extracted its toll. That is fine. But sixteen sessions in seven days does bear a watchful eye, and this author would be rather less charming should she have cause to write about a runner who accumulated a perfectly tidy training base and then quietly unravelled it on a Thursday. Continue at this precise rate of impeccable dullness. One small enquiry before this column retires: did anything protest from the session? The right foot and right knee have a documented history of making their opinions known, and weight training has opinions of its own. Do report back.\"",
"contract": "<k>tail.headline</k>: \"Recovery weight training — easy discipline held, volume to monitor\"\n<k>tail.next_steps[0].action</k>: \"Continue keeping individual sessions at genuinely easy effort\"\n<k>.next_steps</k>: <v>1 step(s)</v>",
