"voice": "<k>voice_preset</k>: <v>'cornerman'</v>  (warmth <v>5</v> · humor <v>3</v> · directness <v>3</v> · energy <v>4</v>)\n<k>stance_school</k>: <v>polarized</v>\n<k>emphasis</k>: Data↔Sentiment <v>3</v> (balanced) · Process↔Outcome <v>1</v> (strongly Process)\n<k>corpus.school.stance</k>: \"Durability is built by lots of easy aerobic running; the long game beats any single sharp session.\"",
"llmcall": "<k>prompt_id</k>: <v>coach_message_v6</v> · <k>schema</k>: <v>2.0</v>\n<k>message</k>: \"Dear Reader, this column is pleased — if not exactly scandalized — to report that you went for a quiet afternoon walk and did absolutely nothing wrong. An RPE of 3, effort solidly in the recovery column, 72 metres of elevation politely absorbed, and every number behaving itself. A thorough non-event, which is, of course, precisely the point. More noteworthy still: you followed last session's instruction and kept this squarely in easy territory. Your training record has a rather documented history of treating \"easy\" as a loose suggestion rather than a standing order, so this author marks today's compliance with genuine, if restrained, appreciation. The aerobic base demands patience above all; today you supplied it without argument. One small entry for the dossier, in the interest of full disclosure: looking across your comparable recovery outings, the efficiency trend has slipped a modest 3.3%. Nothing yet deserving of a pamphlet — but this author does keep watch. The remedy is boringly simple: continue doing exactly what you did this afternoon. Keep easy sessions genuinely easy, let recovery do its quiet work, and efficiency tends to right itself in time. Your training load sits in fresh condition with one hard session already on the books this week, which makes this walk exactly the sort of unassuming, sensible choice that compounds into durability. Unglamorous. Entirely correct. This author approves. Until next we meet.\"",
"contract": "<k>tail.headline</k>: \"Recovery walk — easy discipline delivered, efficiency trend noted\"\n<k>tail.next_steps[0].action</k>: \"Keep easy sessions genuinely easy\"\n<k>.next_steps</k>: <v>1 step(s)</v>",
