"voice": "<k>voice_preset</k>: <v>'cornerman'</v>  (warmth <v>5</v> · humor <v>3</v> · directness <v>3</v> · energy <v>4</v>)\n<k>stance_school</k>: <v>polarized</v>\n<k>emphasis</k>: —\n<k>corpus.school.stance</k>: \"\"",
"llmcall": "<k>prompt_id</k>: <v>coach_message_v2</v> · <k>schema</k>: <v>2.0</v>\n<k>message</k>: \"This ride answered the question I posed about an hour and a half ago: I asked you to confirm whether the cycling in today's block was staying easy, and the numbers say it wasn't. The 30-minute session ran at a moderate clip — average heart rate of 143.7, roughly 75% of your maximum — which is a clear step above the conversational effort I asked for. Taken together with the walk and rowing earlier, today now sits at around 98 minutes of combined movement, and the final leg ran harder than the first. That's a reasonable training day in isolation, but it's landing on top of five hard sessions this week and twenty activities across seven days. Your 28-day training load is up about 15% from the four weeks before it. That's the bigger picture I keep returning to. I'm not going to lecture you on easy-run discipline — you know the guidance, and you've followed it more often than not — but I do want to name what I'm seeing plainly: moderate is showing up in sessions that were meant to be easy, and that's precisely where cumulative fatigue quietly builds without announcing itself. No single session is the issue; it's the sum. No RPE logged for this one, so I'm reading entirely from heart rate. If this genuinely felt conversational — light, could-hold-a-full-conversation easy — I'd want to know, because that would shift my read on things. If it felt like real work, that confirms what the HR is showing. The prescription hasn't changed: the next session needs to be actually easy, RPE 2–3, thirty to forty minutes at most. Not close to easy — easy. That's where recovery happens.\"",
"contract": "<k>tail.headline</k>: \"Moderate indoor ride confirms cycling-creep concern — cumulative load needs a genuine easy session\"\n<k>tail.next_steps[0].action</k>: \"Keep next session genuinely easy\"\n<k>.next_steps</k>: <v>1 step(s)</v>",
