"voice": "<k>voice_preset</k>: <v>'cornerman'</v>  (warmth <v>5</v> · humor <v>3</v> · directness <v>3</v> · energy <v>4</v>)\n<k>stance_school</k>: <v>polarized</v>\n<k>emphasis</k>: —\n<k>corpus.school.stance</k>: \"\"",
"llmcall": "<k>prompt_id</k>: <v>coach_message_v2</v> · <k>schema</k>: <v>2.0</v>\n<k>message</k>: \"Cardiac control on this one was genuinely impressive. Your HR actually drifted *down* by the end — finishing at -1.2% against your personal norm of around +4% for comparable tempo efforts on flat terrain. That's more than 5 percentage points below what you typically do in these conditions, which tells you the aerobic engine was well in command at this pace. Your RPE of 5 sitting right in line with the data is a clean signal too — no daylight between what you felt and what was actually happening. That fits a real trend. Across 11 comparable tempo sessions, your efficiency has improved roughly 9%, and your HR drift at threshold has come down dramatically. The fitness is genuine and it's accumulating. Here's where I have to be straight with you, though. About 75 minutes before this, I said keep the next session easy before returning to hard work — and this came out at a solid tempo effort, your fourth hard session of the week. You paired it with a rowing block on top. I'm not going to hammer on it, but I'd be doing you a disservice if I let it pass: 17 activities in the last seven days, four of them hard, and this was back-to-back within the same afternoon. The fact that today's execution was clean doesn't change the accumulation picture — it might even disguise it a little. The next session or two genuinely needs to be easy. Conversational pace, RPE 2–3, 20 to 30 minutes if you go at all. Not as a formality — the adaptation from this kind of work consolidates during recovery, and without it you're spending rather than saving. The fitness is there. Give it somewhere to land.\"",
"contract": "<k>tail.headline</k>: \"Excellent cardiac control, but fourth hard session in a week warrants genuine recovery\"\n<k>tail.next_steps[0].action</k>: \"Keep next sessions genuinely easy\"\n<k>.next_steps</k>: <v>1 step(s)</v>",
