"beliefs": "<v>DISABLED</v> — COACH_BELIEFS_ENABLED defaults off (PR #403).\nEmits the empty new-runner form; no belief is read or written.\nStored rows kept intact for a recalibrated re-enable (#401).",
"narrative": "<v>DISABLED</v> — COACH_NARRATIVE_ENABLED defaults off (PR #403).\nThe section is empty; the Consolidation job never enqueues. (#402 recalibrates.)",
"voice": "<k>voice_preset</k>: <v>'cornerman'</v>  (warmth <v>5</v> · humor <v>3</v> · directness <v>3</v> · energy <v>4</v>)\n<k>stance_school</k>: <v>polarized</v>\n<k>emphasis</k>: —\n<k>corpus.school.stance</k>: \"\"",
"llmcall": "<k>prompt_id</k>: <v>coach_message_v2</v> · <k>schema</k>: <v>2.0</v>\n<k>message</k>: \"The fuller picture is worth unpacking. That HR drift of -7.1% isn't just \"your heart rate went down\" — it's more than double your personal norm for comparable easy sessions (typically around -2.9% for efforts like this), meaning you genuinely finished fresher than usual. And it wasn't a flat stroll: 94 metres of elevation scattered across 5km meant your body was doing real work, and it still came through that comfortably. Your RPE of 1 lines up exactly with the data — no gap between how it felt and what the numbers show. Both stories are the same. The broader context is worth naming. Your volume and activity count over the past 28 days have roughly tripled compared to the 28 days before that, and this week alone had four hard sessions. That's a heavy block. These two easy days aren't soft filler — the negative drift across both of them is the measurable sign that your system is actually recovering. The body is doing what it's supposed to do. One thing I'm keeping an eye on: across your last 13 comparable easy sessions, your efficiency — roughly, the distance covered per beat of heart rate effort — has been drifting down about 4.5%. That's not alarming on its own, and it makes sense after a load spike of this size, but it is a reason not to rush the return to hard work. With four hard sessions already this week, I'd lean toward one more easy effort before anything genuinely demanding. Let it catch up first.\"",
"contract": "<k>tail.headline</k>: \"Better-than-norm HR drift — high load and declining efficiency warrant patience\"\n<k>tail.next_steps[0].action</k>: \"Keep the next session easy before returning to hard work\"\n<k>.next_steps</k>: <v>1 step(s)</v>",
