"llmcall": "<k>prompt_id</k>: <v>coach_message_v2</v> · <k>schema</k>: <v>2.0</v>\n<k>message</k>: \"You followed through on the easy day, which is exactly what I asked for after yesterday's tempo — good. This walk did its job cleanly: RPE 1, heart rate sitting around 127 bpm with virtually no drift at all (-0.1%), and no meaningful stress on the system. The left leg tightness you mentioned is worth keeping an eye on. The fact that it loosened as you walked is the better sign — stiffness that eases with movement tends to be less concerning than discomfort that builds as you go. Stay attentive to it over the next day or two. If it's still there before your next run, or sharpens rather than fades, get it looked at before heading into anything harder. Given your history with lower limb issues, it's not something to simply brush past. On the load picture: you've stacked four hard sessions into the past seven days, with the last one only yesterday. This walk helps the balance, but I'd want one more easy or rest day before you go anywhere near tempo effort again. There's nothing to gain from rushing it — the work you've already done this week is banked, and it'll still be there when you're fresh.\"",
